// TERMINAL VELOCITY — FREEFALL — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// TERMINAL VELOCITY as lo-fi that falls into jungle — a game alternate of neon,
// selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the
// live song.
// 
// Terminal velocity is the speed a falling body stops accelerating at, and this remix
// falls. The day floats at half time: a felt piano and the neon cabinet's alloy chime
// play Seseragi at HALF SPEED over warbling Rhodes and a dusty boom-bap. On BEAT 56 —
// the downbeat of bar 15, NEON_MINOR_TURN_BEAT, neon-1's strike and its day-to-night
// change — the floor goes: jungle at 174, the figure in C minor at its own speed, twice
// as fast as a moment ago, on the chime with Peter's square pluck over a Reese and a
// chopped break. Drop two lands on bar 45 (beat 176, neon's second strike) with the
// figure at ALL THREE SPEEDS AT ONCE — a crystal pluck in sixteenths, the chime and
// the square in eighths, felt piano and ice bell at half speed — which fits because
// Seseragi repeats each harmony bar twice.
// 
// The cabinet screen loops bars 1–4 and the level picks the song up where the screen
// leaves it, so the strike lands 10–13 bars (14–18 s) into neon-1 — TERMINAL
// VELOCITY's own lead time, which keeps it ahead of neon-1's first boardable train
// (a train whose flight starts before the turn only flies past).
// 
//   1–4    float — the sweep, then the figure at half speed (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–14   float — the rest of the Seseragi phrase at half speed, lo-fi half time
//   15–30  THE FALL (beat 56) — jungle, C minor: the figure at speed (8), the second
//          theme over the Tron ostinato (8)
//   31–38  breakdown — half time again: the Shibuya melody at half speed
//   39–44  build — Shibuya at speed, the break back; its E♭-minor half again
//   45–52  TERMINAL VELOCITY (beat 176) — the figure at three speeds at once
//   53–60  the second theme over the ostinato in sixteenths, a ride
//   61–68  the figure, the ice bell an octave over the chime — everything
//   69–76  float at night — half time, the minor figure at half speed; G7alt and
//          the minor sweep; the loop returns to bar 15
// 
// The melody is TERMINAL VELOCITY's own, note for note, at three speeds: the Seseragi
// figure major and minor with its cadence, the second theme (neon bars 29–36), the
// Tron ostinato, the Shibuya melody and both sweeps. Seseragi and the Shibuya melody
// are JR East's — the clearing caveat on neon.js carries over to this file unchanged.
// 
// 76 bars at 174. Written by work/local/_neon-remix-freefall.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — LIGHTNING (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-picture.mjs): a sixteenth of the whole mix
// overdriven and crushed on bar 45's downbeat, the strike at beat 176 the game flashes every pass.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the lo-fi Rhodes and piano fade under the jungle as it fades in for the fall (13–14); at 67–70 the jungle fades back into the lo-fi.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
